dracon (1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging, split into three binary packages:
    - dracon-server: the daemon, its systemd service and sysusers.d entry,
      and the core configuration (server.conf and friends).
    - dracon-mod-staticcontent: the bundled static file plugin and its
      static_files.conf.
    - libdracon-dev: the header-only plugin API and the CMake package
      config, for building plugins against an installed Dracon.
  * The packaged server.conf (debian/patches) defaults to port 80, with
    HTTPS configured for 443 but left disabled since no certificate is
    shipped; dracon.service already carries CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for it.
  * dracon-mod-staticcontent ships the default landing page from www/ as
    /usr/share/dracon/www and its postinst copies it into /var/www when that
    directory is missing or still empty, so a fresh install answers "/" with
    something instead of a 404. An administrator's own content is never
    touched: the copy is skipped as soon as /var/www holds anything.
  * Added python3-certbot-dracon (built from certbot-dracon/ via pybuild
    alongside the CMake build): a combined Certbot authenticator and
    installer plugin, so "certbot run --configurator dracon -d example.com"
    obtains a certificate, installs it into /etc/dracon, enables HTTPS in
    server.conf, and restarts dracon.service.

 -- BogDan Vatra <bogdan@kde.org>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 17:03:47 +0300
